REGEDIT4

; wined3d's GL card database does not recognise the eGPU's renderer string
; ("NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti/PCIe/SSE2"), so DXGI falls back to its oldest
; NVIDIA entry and reports a GeForce GTX 470 from 2010 -- which is what
; VirtualDJ shows in its "Stems GPU" dropdown, and what it gates the GPU stem
; engine on. Claiming an RTX 4060 Ti 16GB (the newest 16 GB NVIDIA card in
; Wine's table) keeps that gate open.
;
; This only changes the *identity* wined3d reports. It does not select a GPU:
; win32u's display devices already name the real RTX 5060 Ti, and vkd3d binds
; whatever physical device the Vulkan loader offers it. Wine 11 has no
; VideoDescription knob -- the name is looked up from the PCI ID.

[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Wine\Direct3D]
"VideoPciVendorID"=dword:000010de
"VideoPciDeviceID"=dword:00002805
